{
  "semantics": {
    "attributes": {
      "final": {},
      "header": {}
    },
    "blocks": [
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Spring provides a STOMP over WebSocket client and a STOMP over TCP client."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "To begin, you can create and configure "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "WebSocketStompClient"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", as the following example shows:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "listing",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "WebSocketClient webSocketClient = new StandardWebSocketClient();\nWebSocketStompClient stompClient = new WebSocketStompClient(webSocketClient);\nstompClient.setMessageConverter(new StringMessageConverter());\nstompClient.setTaskScheduler(taskScheduler); // for heartbeats"
          }
        ],
        "language": "java",
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "In the preceding example, you could replace "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "StandardWebSocketClient"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " with "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "SockJsClient"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", since that is also an implementation of "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "WebSocketClient"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ". The "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "SockJsClient"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " can use WebSocket or HTTP-based transport as a fallback. For more details, see "
          },
          {
            "inlines": [
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "SockJsClient"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              }
            ],
            "kind": "xref",
            "target": "web/websocket/fallback.html#websocket-fallback-sockjs-client"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Next, you can establish a connection and provide a handler for the STOMP session, as the following example shows:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "listing",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "String url = \"ws://127.0.0.1:8080/endpoint\";\nStompSessionHandler sessionHandler = new MyStompSessionHandler();\nstompClient.connect(url, sessionHandler);"
          }
        ],
        "language": "java",
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "When the session is ready for use, the handler is notified, as the following example shows:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "listing",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "public class MyStompSessionHandler extends StompSessionHandlerAdapter {\n\n\t@Override\n\tpublic void afterConnected(StompSession session, StompHeaders connectedHeaders) {\n\t\t// ...\n\t}\n}"
          }
        ],
        "language": "java",
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Once the session is established, any payload can be sent and is serialized with the configured "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "MessageConverter"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", as the following example shows:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "listing",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "session.send(\"/topic/something\", \"payload\");"
          }
        ],
        "language": "java",
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "You can also subscribe to destinations. The "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "subscribe"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " methods require a handler for messages on the subscription and returns a "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Subscription"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " handle that you can use to unsubscribe. For each received message, the handler can specify the target "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Object"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " type to which the payload should be deserialized, as the following example shows:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "listing",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "session.subscribe(\"/topic/something\", new StompFrameHandler() {\n\n\t@Override\n\tpublic Type getPayloadType(StompHeaders headers) {\n\t\treturn String.class;\n\t}\n\n\t@Override\n\tpublic void handleFrame(StompHeaders headers, Object payload) {\n\t\t// ...\n\t}\n\n});"
          }
        ],
        "language": "java",
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "To enable STOMP heartbeat, you can configure "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "WebSocketStompClient"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " with a "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "TaskScheduler"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " and optionally customize the heartbeat intervals (10 seconds for write inactivity, which causes a heartbeat to be sent, and 10 seconds for read inactivity, which closes the connection)."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "WebSocketStompClient"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " sends a heartbeat only in case of inactivity, i.e. when no other messages are sent. This can present a challenge when using an external broker since messages with a non-broker destination represent activity but aren’t actually forwarded to the broker. In that case you can configure a "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "TaskScheduler"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " when initializing the "
          },
          {
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "External Broker"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "xref",
            "target": "web/websocket/stomp/handle-broker-relay.html"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " which ensures a heartbeat is forwarded to the broker also when only messages with a non-broker destination are sent."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "admonition",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "When you use "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "WebSocketStompClient"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " for performance tests to simulate thousands of clients from the same machine, consider turning off heartbeats, since each connection schedules its own heartbeat tasks and that is not optimized for a large number of clients running on the same machine."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null,
        "type": "note"
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The STOMP protocol also supports receipts, where the client must add a "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "receipt"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " header to which the server responds with a RECEIPT frame after the send or subscribe are processed. To support this, the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "StompSession"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " offers "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "setAutoReceipt(boolean)"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " that causes a "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "receipt"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " header to be added on every subsequent send or subscribe event. Alternatively, you can also manually add a receipt header to the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "StompHeaders"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ". Both send and subscribe return an instance of "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Receiptable"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " that you can use to register for receipt success and failure callbacks. For this feature, you must configure the client with a "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "TaskScheduler"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " and the amount of time before a receipt expires (15 seconds by default)."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Note that "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "StompSessionHandler"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " itself is a "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "StompFrameHandler"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", which lets it handle ERROR frames in addition to the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "handleException"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " callback for exceptions from the handling of messages and "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "handleTransportError"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " for transport-level errors including "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "ConnectionLostException"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "You can use the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "inboundMessageSizeLimit"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " and "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "outboundMessageSizeLimit"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " properties of "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "WebSocketStompClient"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " to limit the maximum size of inbound and outbound WebSocket messages. When an outbound STOMP message exceeds the limit, it is split into partial frames, which the receiver would have to reassemble. By default, there is no size limit for outbound messages. When an inbound STOMP message size exceeds the configured limit, a "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "StompConversionException"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " is thrown. The default size limit for inbound messages is "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "64KB"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "listing",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "WebSocketClient webSocketClient = new StandardWebSocketClient();\nWebSocketStompClient stompClient = new WebSocketStompClient(webSocketClient);\nstompClient.setInboundMessageSizeLimit(64 * 1024); // 64KB\nstompClient.setOutboundMessageSizeLimit(64 * 1024); // 64KB"
          }
        ],
        "language": "java",
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      }
    ],
    "outline": null,
    "title": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "value": "STOMP Client"
      }
    ]
  }
}
